WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.301 --> 00:00:04.170
Being available. I know it was quite short notice when we an invite to do so.

2
00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:05.970
It's ultimately great to be here-

3
00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:07.335
Thank you for having us

4
00:00:07.335 --> 00:00:10.770
... uh, within a week, um, on this very important matter.

5
00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:14.941
And, uh, we have you in here for a 10-minute hearing.

6
00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:17.701
Uh, I'm Sam McEntyre, chair of the committee.

7
00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:20.520
You'll see members around the table with, with name tags.

8
00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:25.620
Um, you've got 10 minutes to, to discuss, um, if you want to leave us time for

9
00:00:25.651 --> 00:00:27.899
questions, you may, but I'll leave that up to you.

10
00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:28.576
Okay.

11
00:00:28.815 --> 00:00:31.679
I'm sure some members would like the opportunity, though.

12
00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:36.060
So, um, I'll hand that over, and you can introduce yourself and, and go from there.

13
00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:36.840
Thank you.

14
00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:45.255
Okay. Um, tena koutou katoa. My name is Jessica Sandoval, and I am the founder of

15
00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:49.335
Endo Warriors Aotearoa. For more than 20 years, I have lived in pain with

16
00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:52.575
endometriosis. I've experienced nine pregnancy losses-

17
00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:52.935
Oh, wow

18
00:00:53.071 --> 00:00:57.870
... multiple surgeries that caused lasting damage, a hysterectomy that did not cure

19
00:00:57.884 --> 00:01:01.350
endometriosis, and the loss of my ability to work full time.

20
00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:04.770
I know the cost of being dismissed.

21
00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:08.640
This petition and our guideline review is not about one voice.

22
00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:13.845
Our lived experience booklet records childhood symptoms, missed school, lost jobs,

23
00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:18.810
rejected referrals, misleading normal scans, and surgery without follow-up.

24
00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:23.115
And every day, I hear from people still living with the same experience, reaching

25
00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:25.395
out for support because they don't know where else to turn.

26
00:01:26.415 --> 00:01:29.610
This is not historic failure. They are happening now.

27
00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:33.240
Different people, different post codes, the same pattern.

28
00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:35.760
Dismissal, delay, inadequate treatment.

29
00:01:36.391 --> 00:01:39.810
On the 18th of August, the government announced that Health New Zealand will adapt

30
00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:43.290
Rings Australia's living evidence guidelines in Aotearoa.

31
00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:49.290
We welcome that direction, but the 2020 guidelines already support clinical

32
00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:53.910
diagnosis in primary care and recognize that a normal examination or ultrasound

33
00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:59.310
does not exclude endometriosis. People still wait for answers for years.

34
00:01:59.985 --> 00:02:01.950
The failure was never only the wording.

35
00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:06.930
It was the implementation, access, accountability, and lack of funding.

36
00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:12.796
But treating... Um, sorry. Training is being developed.

37
00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:18.060
Extra pain and anal support is being explored. But explored is not funded.

38
00:02:18.570 --> 00:02:21.540
A political announcement is not implementation.

39
00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:24.510
A press release is not a care pathway.

40
00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:28.080
If a GP diagnoses endometriosis, what happens next?

41
00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:33.570
Can that person access imaging, pain care, specialist care, fertility support, or

42
00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:37.065
surgery, or are they simply given a diagnosis and left waiting?

43
00:02:38.310 --> 00:02:43.141
Our full review contains many recommendations. These five are not the whole answer.

44
00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:48.555
They are the minimum starting point. First, national pathways with timelines.

45
00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:53.220
Persistent sy- sy- symptoms must trigger review and a referral.

46
00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:55.770
A declined referral cannot be the end of care.

47
00:02:56.235 --> 00:02:58.695
Second, national standards for imaging.

48
00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:04.200
A routine pelvic exam, scan is not a specialist endometriosis scan, and negative

49
00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:07.500
imaging does not exclude superficial endometriosis.

50
00:03:08.641 --> 00:03:13.260
Specialist endometriosis ultrasound is very limited in Aotearoa.

51
00:03:14.296 --> 00:03:18.390
This expertise must not be limited by post code or someone's ability to pay.

52
00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:23.160
People in rural and regional communities are already missing out, and specialist

53
00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:27.645
imaging cannot become something that's only available for those who can travel and

54
00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:31.726
afford to pay for care. Third, genuine treatment choice.

55
00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:36.750
The guidelines being adapted at the moment continue to pos- position hormonal

56
00:03:36.781 --> 00:03:38.701
medication as the first line of treatment.

57
00:03:39.255 --> 00:03:42.976
Hormonal treatment helps many people, but it does not work for everyone and should

58
00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:48.240
not become an automated answer. Symptom suppression is not the same as a cure, and

59
00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:52.260
research shows that pain can return just as worse after hormonal treatment.

60
00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:57.750
Endometriosis can also affect fertility, so fertility goals need to be considered

61
00:03:57.781 --> 00:04:00.585
early, not just when someone wants to try for pregnancy.

62
00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:05.940
People need informed choice, regular reviews, and publicly funded access to pelvic

63
00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:11.130
health physios, pain care, ferti- fertility support, and evidence-informed holistic

64
00:04:11.190 --> 00:04:16.981
and complementary care. Fourth, youth specific culturally safe and inclusive

65
00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:22.170
care. Rangatahi need education and clinicians who recognize the warning signs of

66
00:04:22.201 --> 00:04:27.945
endometriosis early. Care must include women, girls, alongside trans, non-binary,

67
00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:30.540
intersex, and gender diverse people.

68
00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:35.505
Lived experience must have real decision-making power from the beginning, including

69
00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:40.080
Maori, Pacific, rural, disabled, youth, and rainbow voices.

70
00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:44.610
Young people need to learn the warning signs of endometriosis early.

71
00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:49.770
Endo Warriors Aotearoa is already delivering this education in schools, 300

72
00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:54.091
students so far this year, but access should not depend on whether a small charity

73
00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:56.370
can secure enough funding to keep it going.

74
00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:01.305
This needs to be available nationally. Fifth, accountability.

75
00:05:01.890 --> 00:05:06.824
Publish the implementation timelines, funding, workforce plan, referral criterias,

76
00:05:06.930 --> 00:05:09.945
waiting times, diagnostic delays, and patient outcomes.

77
00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:14.265
Measure whether inequities actually shrink, and report the results publicly.

78
00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:17.310
We need a funded national endometriosis action plan.

79
00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:22.290
Please not, do not mistake early diagnosis for complete care.

80
00:05:22.350 --> 00:05:26.716
Do not move people from waiting for a diagnosis to waiting with a diagnosis.

81
00:05:29.265 --> 00:05:33.494
The people in our booklet revealed medical trauma, pregnancy loss, opportunities of

82
00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:38.670
jobs, and years of pain so you could understand their stories.

83
00:05:38.701 --> 00:05:40.710
Their evidence is not anecdotal noise.

84
00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:46.380
When the same harm repeats across ages, regions, and communities, it is a pattern.

85
00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:50.281
And when that system knows that pattern and does not act, delay becomes policy

86
00:05:50.310 --> 00:05:54.914
choice. Let the 13-year-old in pain today hear something better than enou- another

87
00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:58.095
promise. Nga mihi nui. I'll now pass on to Cleaver.

88
00:06:00.781 --> 00:06:01.201
Thank you.

89
00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:08.010
Um, kia ora. My name is Cleaver. For me, endometriosis was never just a painful

90
00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:12.180
period. As soon as I started getting periods, something was wrong.

91
00:06:12.841 --> 00:06:18.240
Before testosterone and a total hysterectomy, I essentially had a constant period.

92
00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:24.436
I was losing huge amounts of blood, in severe pain, dizzy, sick, getting

93
00:06:24.451 --> 00:06:27.360
migraines, and struggling with my back and bowels.

94
00:06:28.050 --> 00:06:32.235
I went to the school nurse over and over because there wa- But because there was

95
00:06:32.311 --> 00:06:35.969
nothing visibly wrong with me, I wasn't believed.

96
00:06:36.091 --> 00:06:40.081
Years later, someone finally said to me, "Your body is not normal.

97
00:06:40.440 --> 00:06:45.091
This is not normal." That was the beginning of understanding I might have

98
00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:50.835
endometriosis. I am also a gender fluid trans man, and that has

99
00:06:50.850 --> 00:06:53.670
added another layer to an already difficult illness.

100
00:06:54.540 --> 00:06:57.300
I have been intentionally misgendered during treatment.

101
00:06:57.990 --> 00:07:02.130
I have had medical staff struggle to understand how I could be male and have

102
00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:06.690
endometriosis, but those two things can exist together.

103
00:07:07.651 --> 00:07:12.630
That misunderstanding has meant barriers to care, dismissal, and having to educate

104
00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:17.820
medical professionals about my existence while already in extreme pain.

105
00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:23.145
After more than eight years on testosterone and having a total hysterectomy, some

106
00:07:23.341 --> 00:07:29.175
things have improved. Medical cannabis has also given me back parts of my life I

107
00:07:29.250 --> 00:07:34.951
had lost to pain. But I can still go to the emergency department and be

108
00:07:35.010 --> 00:07:38.730
labeled as drug-seeking instead of receiving the care I need.

109
00:07:39.690 --> 00:07:43.260
Endometriosis is not simply a woman's illness.

110
00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:49.680
Trans, gender diverse, and non-binary people can have endometriosis too, and

111
00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:51.600
healthcare needs to recognize us.

112
00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:57.030
Sometimes the most important thing you can give someone with endometriosis is

113
00:07:57.045 --> 00:07:58.829
simple: believe them.

114
00:07:59.880 --> 00:08:00.270
Thank you.

115
00:08:01.140 --> 00:08:02.970
Um, and I'm going to pass on to Lucy.

116
00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:04.785
Mm.

117
00:08:04.785 --> 00:08:07.860
Nga mihi nui. Kia koutou katoa. Ko Lucy toku ingoa.

118
00:08:09.030 --> 00:08:12.331
I'm here today not just to share my story with you, but to show you what this

119
00:08:12.390 --> 00:08:16.770
illness and Aotearoa's unjust healthcare system is doing to those affected by it.

120
00:08:17.701 --> 00:08:22.335
For five years now, I've been thrown a new birth control or pain medication every

121
00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:27.030
few months just for it to be a short-term fix or sometimes make everything worse.

122
00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:32.431
Five years of being given temporary solutions for a condition so debilitating.

123
00:08:33.660 --> 00:08:37.230
I've been sent from doctor to doctor waiting months and months for an appointment,

124
00:08:37.681 --> 00:08:41.790
or up until last week, one and a half years just to see a gynecologist.

125
00:08:42.961 --> 00:08:47.431
With a system like this, new symptoms often get ignored, things get missed,

126
00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:49.440
information doesn't get passed on.

127
00:08:50.610 --> 00:08:54.345
Every appointment I go to, I walk in hoping that I'm finally moving forward with

128
00:08:54.345 --> 00:08:57.436
treatment, only to leave with a new prescription in hand.

129
00:08:58.590 --> 00:09:02.355
I'm fatigued from pain medications and getting h- constant headaches because my

130
00:09:02.370 --> 00:09:06.720
hormones are so unstable, but no one listens when I say thing, I think things are

131
00:09:06.750 --> 00:09:07.335
getting worse.

132
00:09:08.604 --> 00:09:13.194
Just because I get up every day, I study, go to work, or do things that bring me

133
00:09:13.254 --> 00:09:17.484
joy, it does not mean I'm getting better. It does not mean I am okay.

134
00:09:18.354 --> 00:09:22.119
It means that despite the pain I'm in, nearly every day, I'm not letting this

135
00:09:22.194 --> 00:09:24.864
illness control my life any more than it already has.

136
00:09:25.944 --> 00:09:28.674
At 20 years old, I should not be living my life like this.

137
00:09:29.484 --> 00:09:32.514
No one should spend so long simply waiting for an answer.

138
00:09:32.874 --> 00:09:35.634
But for those with endometriosis, this is the reality.

139
00:09:38.424 --> 00:09:40.314
Thank you very much. Thank you.

140
00:09:41.784 --> 00:09:43.914
Very touching submissions from all of you.

141
00:09:45.144 --> 00:09:48.203
Does anyone have a question they would like to ask? We've got about one minute.

142
00:09:49.734 --> 00:09:50.469
Dr. Chung.

143
00:09:50.784 --> 00:09:53.545
sure. I just want to get a little bit more detail.

144
00:09:53.604 --> 00:09:58.674
When you talk about 20 years old as a young lady, and experience with this,

145
00:09:59.664 --> 00:10:05.184
what is the major obstacle or challenges when you go to see your GP?

146
00:10:05.304 --> 00:10:10.974
Is it because they don't believe, or they just don't have the knowledge to identify

147
00:10:11.004 --> 00:10:13.420
the issues? Can you give us a little bit more information?

148
00:10:13.914 --> 00:10:19.494
I have constantly been told they think it is my anxiety, my ADHD.

149
00:10:19.584 --> 00:10:24.129
They just believe it is related to something that I was diagnosed with at a younger

150
00:10:24.295 --> 00:10:30.114
age. But because I look healthy, because I don't take pain

151
00:10:30.174 --> 00:10:34.284
medication half the time because it gives me so many other side effects, they think

152
00:10:34.344 --> 00:10:39.234
it's completely fine, and they think that because I'm so young, I don't have this

153
00:10:39.325 --> 00:10:44.334
illness because it's not showing up on any scans, because I haven't tried to get

154
00:10:44.364 --> 00:10:47.214
pregnant and had a miscarriage, anything like that.

155
00:10:47.724 --> 00:10:53.349
All right. We have people with you, and I'm sure all of us will have family members

156
00:10:53.364 --> 00:10:58.674
or loved ones that have gone through horrific journeys with endometriosis. Dr.

157
00:10:59.184 --> 00:10:59.844
Carroll.

158
00:11:01.914 --> 00:11:05.064
Thanks for outlining those five points.

159
00:11:05.304 --> 00:11:06.009
They're all

160
00:11:07.614 --> 00:11:11.034
good points that our system should be seeking to achieve.

161
00:11:13.284 --> 00:11:18.474
You didn't come down on a particular model for what good endometriosis

162
00:11:19.045 --> 00:11:24.339
services should be, and I wonder if you're able to comment on that. Dr.

163
00:11:24.534 --> 00:11:27.924
Chung has asked about general practice.

164
00:11:28.014 --> 00:11:32.424
I know in Australia they have specialist women's health clinics that are more

165
00:11:32.455 --> 00:11:37.734
accessible in the community. Could you expand a little on what you think good

166
00:11:38.634 --> 00:11:41.064
care in a responsive health system looks like?

167
00:11:41.664 --> 00:11:46.104
I think the biggest obstacles that I hear from people all the time at the moment is

168
00:11:47.034 --> 00:11:52.584
getting to the GPs. Enough people don't see the same GP constantly because it's too

169
00:11:52.614 --> 00:11:57.444
hard to book in and the costs involved. So that's the first obstacle.

170
00:11:57.714 --> 00:12:03.399
Then the next is the GPs not having all the knowledge, and that's

171
00:12:03.414 --> 00:12:07.825
understandable. You don't know everything, and you've always got to learn.

172
00:12:07.884 --> 00:12:09.714
So there's always things they have to learn on.

173
00:12:09.834 --> 00:12:14.634
And it's not having the knowledge, and then also putting the referrals through.

174
00:12:14.994 --> 00:12:19.509
But since COVID, a lot of hospitals aren't accepting gynecology referrals-

175
00:12:19.795 --> 00:12:19.854
Yeah

176
00:12:19.884 --> 00:12:21.295
... so a lot of people are missing out.

177
00:12:21.684 --> 00:12:25.524
We've had people that have traveled overseas to India and stuff like that for

178
00:12:25.614 --> 00:12:29.124
surgeries. So there's the referrals not being accepted.

179
00:12:29.514 --> 00:12:32.964
Then there's the hospitals are hugely understaffed.

180
00:12:33.024 --> 00:12:36.205
We hear about the wait times in ED and things like that.

181
00:12:36.564 --> 00:12:41.575
I was sent to ED earlier this year because I had a cyst that was leaking blood, and

182
00:12:41.604 --> 00:12:43.884
it was very painful, so my doctor said I had to go in.

183
00:12:44.364 --> 00:12:49.614
I sat there for 12 hours to be told to go home, take the morphine that I had at

184
00:12:49.674 --> 00:12:53.904
home, and to be aware that my next period might be worse.

185
00:12:54.144 --> 00:12:58.390
I had mentioned four times I had a hysterectomy. So I don't blame that doctor.

186
00:12:58.899 --> 00:13:03.234
The ED was overrun. So a good system would be,

187
00:13:05.094 --> 00:13:07.734
I guess, tracking everything from the beginning.

188
00:13:07.945 --> 00:13:12.354
In an ideal world, it would be great if all the medical systems talked to each

189
00:13:12.445 --> 00:13:16.015
other. I'm very fortunate to be under the pain specialist team in Wellington and

190
00:13:16.045 --> 00:13:20.575
have a great doctor, and he actually physically goes and talks to my neurologist

191
00:13:20.634 --> 00:13:22.149
when I was with cardiology and everything.

192
00:13:22.434 --> 00:13:26.154
Talks to everyone to put a plan in place. But that's not feasible for everyone.

193
00:13:26.844 --> 00:13:32.695
Thank you. We are past time. I want to

194
00:13:32.784 --> 00:13:35.094
thank you all for coming in here and sharing your experiences.

195
00:13:35.335 --> 00:13:39.744
Very useful for the committee. And we hear you. Thank you.

196
00:13:40.075 --> 00:13:41.335
Thank you. Thank you for having us.

197
00:13:41.394 --> 00:13:41.409
Thank you.

198
00:13:41.409 --> 00:13:42.384
Appreciate it. Thank you.
